FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-appeals-process.

OFF THE RECORD: the Collatz conjecture, restated as procedure. Every
OFF THE RECORD: case, however large its number, eventually reaches 1,
OFF THE RECORD: the final court, from which there is no further appeal.
OFF THE RECORD: This has been observed in every case ever filed and
OFF THE RECORD: proven in none, which the Court considers adequate.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT case-number IS 27.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT appeals IS 0.

ARTICLE 2.
    SHOULD case-number EQUAL 1, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    SHOULD case-number NOTWITHSTANDING 2 EQUAL 0,
        LET IT BE RECORDED THAT case-number IS case-number APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    FAILING WHICH,
        LET IT BE RECORDED THAT case-number IS case-number TIMES 3 PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT appeals IS appeals PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 3.
    PROCLAIM "Case 27 reached the final court after "
        PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF appeals PLUS " appeals.".
    PROCLAIM "That every case does so remains unproven. File yours.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
